  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#transparent-content-models\r\n\r\n> For instance, an ins element inside a ruby element cannot contain an rt element, because the part of the ruby element's content model that allows ins elements is the part that allows phrasing content, and the rt element is not phrasing content\\.\r\n\r\nI think this example would be less opaque if it included a bit more information about the mentioned elements directly in the example; at least, it should probably mention that the `ins` elements content model is transparent.  (You know, like the other example in this section does.)",
